WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:17.325
Other required equipment includes navigation lights and sound-signaling equipment that meet the Navigation Rules, the oil discharge and garbage placards on boats twenty-six feet and over, and a Coast Guard certified marine sanitation device if you have an installed toilet.

2
00:00:17.575 --> 00:00:25.175
Before every trip, brief your passengers on where the life jackets are, how to put them on, and what to do in an emergency.

3
00:00:25.425 --> 00:00:39.625
Beyond the minimum, a professional captain carries a registered EPIRB or personal locator beacon, a VHF radio with DSC, a well-stocked first aid kit, and reliable bilge pumps with a high-water alarm.
